   "evidence": "Definition body: `ChainComplex.of (fun i \u21a6 ModuleCat.of K (Fin (n i) \u2192 K)) (fun i \u21a6 ModuleCat.ofHom (Matrix.toLin' ((LinearMap.toMatrix (c (i + 1)) (c i) ...).map \u03c6)))`. The module docstring calls it the 'coordinate model of the scalar extension `K \u2297_A C`'. Mathlib uses `baseChange` for tensor-product constructions, e.g. `LinearMap.baseChange`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Algebra/Homology/ReidemeisterTorsion/Componentwise.lean",
   "fix": "Rename to a coordinate-specific name such as `matrixBaseChange` (with `matrixBaseChangeBasis`, `toMatrix_matrixBaseChange_d`), and apply the same rename in `reidemeisterTorsion_eq_reidemeisterTorsion_baseChange`, `map_reidemeisterTorsion_baseChange`, `reidemeisterTorsion_baseChange_id` and `reidemeisterTorsion_baseChange_eq_of_toMatrix_eq`.",
   "issue": "`HomologicalComplex.baseChange` names a basis-dependent coordinate model (`Fin (n i) \u2192 K` with the differential matrices mapped entrywise, only for \u2124-graded `ModuleCat` chain complexes) with the generic Mathlib term for scalar extension (`LinearMap.baseChange`, tensor product). That misleads readers and claims the name a canonical `K \u2297_A C` complex (via `ModuleCat.extendScalars`) would need.",
   "line": 107
  }
